# Local runtime data and teacher-specific configuration
data/*
!data/crm-cookies.example.json
!data/fetch-new-class-student-list.mjs
!data/new-class-group-send-cancel-config.json
!data/workbench-update-source.example.json
!data/workbench-update-source.json

# Browser login profiles / cookies
.chrome-debug-profile/
.chrome-crm-listen-profile/
.chrome-dingtalk-profile/

# Python / Node generated files
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Local logs and archives
tmp/
artifacts/
*.log
*.zip

# Local Codex skills are never committed: they may contain old cookies, private
# workspace memory, and a hardcoded WorkBuddy ACCESS_TOKEN (sync.py). The
# workbench ships skills via the local zip package (codemao_teacher_workbench_template.zip),
# which is built from disk and is NOT affected by git ignore rules.
#
# IMPORTANT (2026-08-27): the "send finished feedback" task loads
#   skills/codemao-makeup-reminder/scripts/create_makeup_reminder.py
# at runtime, so distributed teachers MUST have skills/ on disk. The zip-based
# install provides it. If GitHub becomes the only distribution channel, first
# remove the hardcoded ACCESS_TOKEN from skills/codemao-course-data/sync.py and
# move credentials to config, then whitelist skills/ code files here.
skills/

# Monthly-exam assets (award template, CJK font, per-question explanation
# images, voice templates) are committed so teachers get them via git update.
